WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:00.880
Good morning, John.

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.440
Is it me or has my videos been crazy boring lately?

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.960
I just don't think that I do enough jump cuts anymore.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.640
My friends, you are correct!

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.420
This should be a John Green day, but it is not.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.700
That's right, it's a Hank Green day!

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.520
Hello, everyone.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.260
I've taken this particular John Green Tuesday in exchange for John doing the next two Tuesdays in a row,

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.020
and for getting John Green, a professional New York Times bestselling author,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.500
to proofread the first section of my novel, which I just finished.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.920
The first section, not the whole novel, but that's exciting anyway.

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.680
I mean, I managed to write like a hundred and fifty pages of this book!

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.960
Now I get a professional author to proofread it for me.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.820
Isn't brotherhood fantastic?

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.280
John, on Thursday, you brought back the Evil Baby Orphanage and yes,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:45.200
It is true, we have some very large differences of opinion of how the evil baby orphanage should be approached,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.440
more as a story than as an actual entity.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.200
John wants there to be well-known evil babies in the Evil Baby Orphanage,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.900
so, like, he wants Evil Baby Stalin and Evil Baby Hitler, and he wants all these people interacting

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.140
but my problem with that is that if you've got all the evil babies in the Evil Baby Orphanage,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.920
why does the world still suck so much!?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.420
Which is why, from my personal perspective,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.400
I'm much more intrigued by the idea that there is an Evil Baby Orphanage out there already,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.020
and the guy who created it is just too busy and out of his mind trying to fix the world in all these ways,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.800
that this is currently, what we're living in right now, is the best that he can do.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.340
But that, of course, is neither here nor there

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.060
because John, you asked the Nerdfighters to create a time machine,

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.780
and I've been thinking about precisely how that might be done.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.680
There are two major problems with time travel.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.620
First, if you do it you have the possibility of creating the Grandfather Paradox,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.400
which might unravel the universe, which would suck.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.920
The Grandfather Paradox, of course, being

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.480
that if I go back and kill my grandfather, than how did he die, because I was never born.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.080
That just seems like a loophole that the universe wouldn't allow.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.880
The second problem with time travel is that if it was possible,

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.160
why don't we ever see any time travelers?

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.500
I'd want to come back to the dawn of the information age

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.760
and watch the decline of television and the rise of YouTube!

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.260
I mean, that's exactly where I'd want to be, anywhere in history: right here.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.940
There are several types of time travel that would exclude the Grandfather Paradox

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.080
and explain why we aren't always inundated by time tourists.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.780
The first of these is the easiest way of time traveling and we all can do it together right now.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.920
Now what I want you to do is look right here.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:02.620
Right around there.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.600
You, my friend, are traveling forward in time at one second per second.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.140
Oh, I just blew my own mind!

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.640
The problem is making that go backwards or forwards faster.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.960
Turns out making it go forwards faster isn't even all that difficult!

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.760
You just have to move really fast!

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.060
*hank noises*

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.840
Unfortunately I don't think that that was fast enough and now I have a little bit of a headache.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.100
But if you could go really fast, like close to the speed of light fast,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.740
then suddenly you experience time as traveling at the same rate,

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.680
but relative to other people, your time is traveling much more slowly.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.180
Fans of science fiction literature will know all the freak about this,

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.180
but if you take an interstellar journey at near the speed of light,

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.340
by the time you get to your destination maybe only a couple of years will have passed for you,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.880
but tens or hundreds or even thousands of years could have passed for the rest of the universe.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.580
Unfortunately, this doesn't actually help us travel backwards in time, only forwards in time,

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.500
and only sorta-kinda-a-little-bit does it help us travel forward in time.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.860
But there is a way to use that phenomenon to then bridge

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.840
the place that's forward in time and the place that's back in time.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.540
Basically you create a wormhole, which we don't actually know how to do,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.420
but many people say that it is theoretically possible.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.240
So you create this wormhole which bridges two places in the universe,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.900
then you take one of the ends of that wormhole, and you move it very fast at close to the speed of light.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.100
Now for that end of the wormhole, time is traveling very very slowly,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.960
but for the other end of the wormhole, time is traveling at absolutely normal speeds.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.040
So then at the end of the process you stop the wormholes,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.580
and suddenly if you enter one end of the wormhole,

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.500
you either come out dead, or you come out back in time.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.880
But if I created the time machine today, I couldn't go back in time to kill my grandfather,

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.580
because I could only go back to today.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.820
Forever I could go back to today, but I could never go back any further than that.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.920
And so, my friends, for the Evil Baby Orphanage,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.340
this means that every day the universe spends without a time machine,

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.520
is another day that evil babies will be free to do their evil on our world...!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.800
Shoot.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.700
Please, in comments, let me know if there are other opportunities for backwards time travel,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.560
and I would really like to hear whether you're on John's side or my side of the Evil Baby Orphanage debate.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.060
Should they be historical evil babies or non-historical evil babies?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.160
Everyone will see me tomorrow with my Song Wednesday song.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.340
DFTBA.

